# Aircall Team Management System

A secure web application for managing Aircall team memberships with role-based access control.

## 🔐 Security Features

- **3-Layer Authentication:**
  1. Netlify site-wide password protection
  2. Individual user authentication via CSV
  3. Aircall API credentials (not stored in code)

- **Role-Based Access:**
  - **Admin:** Can manage users and access admin panel
  - **User:** Can only manage team assignments

- **Audit Trail:**
  - All changes are logged
  - Track who made what changes and when
  - Download change logs as CSV

## 📁 Files Included

- `index.html` - Main team management interface
- `admin.html` - Admin panel for user management
- `User_List.csv` - User credentials and permissions (create this)
- `netlify.toml` - Netlify configuration
- `DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md` - Complete setup instructions

## 🚀 Quick Start

1. **Create `User_List.csv`:**
```csv
Email,Password,Team Access,Role
your@email.com,password123,"Team A,Team B",admin
```

2. **Deploy to Netlify:**
   - Drag & drop all files to https://app.netlify.com/drop
   - Or connect your GitHub repository

3. **Enable Password Protection:**
   - Go to Site Settings → Access Control
   - Enable Password Protection under Visitor Access

4. **Share Access:**
   - Site URL
   - Netlify password
   - User credentials (from CSV)
   - API credentials

## 📖 Full Documentation

See `DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md` for complete setup instructions.

## 🎨 Aircall Branding

- Colors: Aircall Green (#00BD82), Accent (#FFC000)
- Clean, minimal interface
- Matches Aircall design language

## ⚙️ Features

- Bulk user assignment to teams
- Search and filter users
- Real-time sync with Aircall
- Change log tracking
- CSV export of changes
- Mobile-responsive design

## 🔄 Updating

Push changes to GitHub → Netlify auto-deploys

## 💡 Tips

- Keep your GitHub repo private
- Rotate API credentials regularly
- Use strong passwords in CSV
- Review change logs periodically
